From: fish <lunarisfelix02@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:50:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] op7t-0167: Wi-Fi: link quality at once on link-up, then every 2 s

0166 works (2026-11-10): wifid logs "Rssi: -63 ... Snr: 32" from event 39
and the status bar shows bars. They should come sooner. Now: the first
event is posted at link-up itself, the next 1 s later, then every 2 s
(was 1 s after link-up, then 5 s). wifid's handler only drops events
under 1 s apart. Per-core RSSI is filled too (both cores = RSSI): wifid
logged "perCoreRssiHistory is Empty!" every event.

Apply after 0166.
---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/redwood_apple80211.c b/bsd/dev/redwood_apple80211.c
index ccd5230..6a054d1 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/redwood_apple80211.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/redwood_apple80211.c
@@ -651,7 +651,7 @@ post(uint32_t code, const void *data, uint32_t length)
  * are not measured here: 54 (Mbit/s) stands for them. wifid drops events that come "too frequent";
  * Apple's drivers send them every few seconds.
  */
-#define LQM_PERIOD_MS           5000u
+#define LQM_PERIOD_MS           2000u     /* 0167: was 5000; wifid ignores only those under 1 s apart */
 
 struct apple80211_weight_avg_lqm {
 	int32_t rssi, snr, tx_rate, rx_rate;
@@ -711,6 +711,8 @@ lqm_post(void)
 		if (full != NULL) {             /* 0166 */
 			full->rssi_valid = 1;
 			full->rssi = lqm.rssi;
+			full->per_core_valid = 1;       /* 0167: wifid logged "perCoreRssiHistory is Empty!" */
+			full->per_core[0] = full->per_core[1] = (int8_t)lqm.rssi;
 			full->snr_valid = 1;
 			full->snr = (int16_t)lqm.snr;
 			full->noise_valid = 1;
@@ -758,8 +760,12 @@ lqm_run(bool on)
 	lqm_running = on;
 	lck_mtx_unlock(&apple80211_lock);
 	if (on) {
-		/* (the first a second after the link: wifid sets up its link-quality state on link-up first) */
-		thread_call_enter_delayed(lqm_call, mach_absolute_time() + lqm_period_abs() / 5);
+		/*
+		 * 0167: the first at once (the bars came a second or more after the link), the next 1 s later in
+		 * case wifid was still setting up its link-quality state for the new link, then every period.
+		 */
+		thread_call_enter_delayed(lqm_call, mach_absolute_time() + lqm_period_abs() / 2);
+		lqm_post();
 	} else {
 		thread_call_cancel(lqm_call);
 	}
